    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0790" n="700" xml:id="pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/207: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Geneva (Gilbert)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-03T12:00:00-05:00">February 3,
                        1932—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>36. For Reber. Penultimate paragraph your
                    telegram 66, February 1, 6 p.m. There is no objection to permitting in your
                    discretion that publicity be given to your memorandum, provided the same
                    procedure is followed with respect to any others on this subject which may have
                    been submitted by other members. Under Geneva date line the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">New York Times</hi> yesterday reported your submission
                    of the memorandum together with an apparently accurate summary. Please send full
                    text by mail.</p>
                <p>When do you anticipate the <hi rendition="#italic">rapporteur</hi> will report to
                    the Council?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
